r hard to hide who you are when someone is fighting you).I am sure this would be relatively easy using shadows() and all. Impersonatewould work in a similar way; allowing the thief to speak in a room asif they were another. For example, you a thief could 'impersonate airborne'followed by the typical message. If successful players would read the message as coming from me instead of you. Failure would give a messagelike 'Herp tries his best to impersonate Airborne and says: ...'Two fun and not unbalancing ideas, and cannot be used in combat.	The last idea would be 'fencing'. Not swordplay, but rather sellingvaluables. The price would reflect the thief's CHR and might give a littleover the common price. Or maybe, you might allow selling of items withvalue over 1000 coins to have a chance of success.	Oh, one more. 'Palming' or the ability to hide an item on ones person.This would either change the short of an item in a players inventory,or mask it entirely. Could be useful.	Well here are some to concider. Enjoy and long live the Thieves.**tmi.ccs.northeastern.edu 5555**> Airborne says: 138.40.11.1 6999 is lpcc.@Spool has gone linkdead.Airborne says: 192.92.115.10 2222 is genocide**  /players/mangla/bin has a test bin in it. It's called _test.c  /players/mangla/guild/guild.c is an inheritable file which capturesplayer cammands checks the /players/mangla/bin directory for the command.If it exsits then it will execute the appropriate function for the player.  /players/mangla/obj/soul.c is the file you need to clone to test _test.c.Notice how short the file is. It never needs to get much bigger than that. Allcommands can be created like _test.c was. And it save quite a bit of memory,since the guild members are sharing the same commands. You don't load a newcommand for every member :)If you have any questions, talk to Scooter. It's his code. :)Mangla**beispiel:  map_array(users(),#'environment())  map_array(usesr(),#'ca